## Fixing the ingest properly

Search-time normalization is a workaround. The durable fix:

```ini
# props.conf
[winevt_json]
INDEXED_EXTRACTIONS = json
KV_MODE = none
TIMESTAMP_FIELDS = winlog.event_time
TIME_FORMAT = %Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%6N%Z
MAX_TIMESTAMP_LOOKAHEAD = 40
SHOULD_LINEMERGE = false
TRUNCATE = 0
```

```ini
# inputs.conf
[monitor:///path/to/json/...]
sourcetype = winevt_json
index = wineventlog
```

Set `KV_MODE = none` when using `INDEXED_EXTRACTIONS = json` — running both double-extracts
and roughly doubles your field count for no benefit.

This requires reindexing to apply to existing data.


index=<your_index> "4624"
| rex field=_raw "^\w{3}\s+\w{3}\s+\d+\s+[\d:]+\s+\d{4}\s+(?<EventID>\d+)\s+(?<SourceName>\S+)"
| where EventID=4624
| rex field=_raw "Logon Type:\s+(?<LogonType>\d+)"
| rex field=_raw "Source Network Address:\s+(?<SrcIp>[^\s\t]+)"
| rex field=_raw "Source Port:\s+(?<SrcPort>\d+)"
| rex field=_raw "Workstation Name:\s+(?<Workstation>[^\s\t]*)"
| rex field=_raw "Logon Process:\s+(?<LogonProcess>[^\s\t]+)"
